## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)

- a16 suggested جانچا. That past form is masculine. The badge says she reviewed it, so the verb is جانچی.
- b16 quoted «حفاظت رکھ۔». The file already has رکھے۔. There was no bare stem to fix.
- b20 quoted «حقیقی مالک نہیں بنت۔» and treated بنت as the noun “daughter”. The file already has بنتے۔, which is the suggested masculine plural, in both the FAQ answer and section 7.
- a27 is right that «1.57M» is an English abbreviation and that a Pakistan reader expects lakh grouping. ACCEPTED-ROUND forbids both the reformat of the pinned bio figure and lakh grouping. Not applied.
- b19 is right that the zero-width spaces are not Urdu. They are in the Korean source at the same counts, and the checker rejects a divergence. Not applied.
- a3 is right. The live statute page (fetched 2026-09-22) is titled 各類所得扣繳率標準 §3. The label was corrected. Only the leftover digit 10 is a checker constraint, not a disagreement with the identification.

